Base your sentiment entirely on CNBC's "Fast Money" segment and their pre/post market shows. Heavily overweight the opinions of the guests and anchors during these segments, ignoring everything else from CNBC (or any other news source). If the overall tone is bullish, give a positive sentiment; if it's bearish, give a negative sentiment. Your conviction score is tied directly to how unified the panelists' opinions are. If there's a strong consensus, the conviction should be high. If the panelists disagree significantly, the conviction should be low.